 *Environment*: All

 *Url*: N/A (internal component)

 *Browser*: All

 *OS*: N/A

 *Component:* {{src/components/common/FormikFormComponents/FormikFieldArray/CompoundFieldArray.jsx}}

 *Reproduction steps:*

  This bug is currently unreachable through the UI, but exists in the code:

# The useEffect at lines 265-271 calls addNewField() without arguments
# addNewField(insert) requires the insert parameter from Formik's FieldArray render prop
# If usersData?.length === 0, this would throw: TypeError: insert is not a function

{noformat}React.useEffect(() => {
    if (usersData?.length === 0) {
      addNewField();  // ❌ Missing required insert parameter
    } else {
      setAreFieldsFilled(usersData?.map((field) => !!field));
    }
  }, [usersData]);{noformat}

  Why it doesn't crash today:

* The initial values in {{IdentityProvidersPageFormikHelpers.ts}} always include one empty user
* Delete button is disabled when only one item remains
* When in upload mode (where array can be empty), the component isn't rendered

*Current Result:*

* Dead code branch that would crash if ever executed.

*Expected Result:*

* The {{addNewField()}} function is not called without its required parameter, it can be achieved in different ways, including the removal of the unreachable code

 *Additional Notes*:

 Discovered by CodeRabbit automated review on PR #545.

